1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,789
RoboDemo. Reconciling demonstration

2
00:00:02,789 --> 00:00:04,809
intent and execution progress

3
00:00:04,809 --> 00:00:06,899
for long-horizon manipulation.

4
00:00:08,350 --> 00:00:10,759
A human demonstration shows a procedure,

5
00:00:10,759 --> 00:00:12,083
not just a final goal.

6
00:00:15,450 --> 00:00:17,512
The reference shows what should happen.

7
00:00:17,512 --> 00:00:19,204
It cannot tell us what the robot

8
00:00:19,204 --> 00:00:20,421
has actually completed.

9
00:00:20,821 --> 00:00:22,984
We preserve the procedure in one memory,

10
00:00:22,984 --> 00:00:25,365
and track completed interactions in another.

11
00:00:28,450 --> 00:00:31,211
Hierarchical sampling combines sparse global

12
00:00:31,211 --> 00:00:33,847
and event frames with a dense motion clip.

13
00:00:34,247 --> 00:00:36,772
Frozen semantic and motion encoders

14
00:00:36,772 --> 00:00:38,792
produce fused memory tokens.

15
00:00:38,792 --> 00:00:42,183
These write Retrieval TTT once, before rollout.

16
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:47,042
The execution branch encodes the new image,

17
00:00:47,042 --> 00:00:49,333
conditioned on the current robot state

18
00:00:49,333 --> 00:00:51,383
and the preceding executed action.

19
00:00:51,783 --> 00:00:53,747
It updates progress memory causally,

20
00:00:53,747 --> 00:00:55,602
without overwriting the reference.

21
00:00:58,450 --> 00:01:00,724
Context tokens write to fast weights.

22
00:01:00,724 --> 00:01:02,567
Action-side queries read them.

23
00:01:02,967 --> 00:01:04,616
Inside each action block,

24
00:01:04,616 --> 00:01:07,452
the expert reads intent first, then refines

25
00:01:07,452 --> 00:01:10,157
that representation with actual progress.

26
00:01:10,557 --> 00:01:11,963
Both memory states remain

27
00:01:11,963 --> 00:01:13,650
fixed during action denoising.

28
00:01:16,450 --> 00:01:18,527
When a human video is unavailable,

29
00:01:18,527 --> 00:01:20,726
Refreward ranks robot demonstrations

30
00:01:20,726 --> 00:01:23,170
using the instruction and initial image.

31
00:01:23,570 --> 00:01:25,106
The selected video enters

32
00:01:25,106 --> 00:01:27,133
the same intent-memory interface.

33
00:01:28,083 --> 00:01:30,245
We first evaluate in simulation.

34
00:01:30,245 --> 00:01:33,285
Across fifty tasks and two thousand episodes,

35
00:01:33,285 --> 00:01:35,244
RoboDemo achieves eighty-four

36
00:01:35,244 --> 00:01:37,001
point six percent success.

37
00:01:37,401 --> 00:01:39,060
The table shows the overall

38
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:40,473
and level-wise results.

39
00:01:41,450 --> 00:01:44,743
Across C15, C30, and C45, mean Seen-task

40
00:01:44,743 --> 00:01:47,871
success is ninety point seven percent.

41
00:01:48,271 --> 00:01:50,490
The robot-reference variant reaches

42
00:01:50,490 --> 00:01:52,328
ninety percent on Seen tasks.

43
00:01:52,328 --> 00:01:54,799
Unseen results are reported separately.

44
00:01:57,450 --> 00:02:00,473
On C15 Seen tasks, mixing both contexts in

45
00:02:00,473 --> 00:02:03,423
one memory reaches seventy-three percent.

46
00:02:03,823 --> 00:02:06,108
Separate memories with cascaded reads

47
00:02:06,108 --> 00:02:08,393
reach eighty-nine point five percent,

48
00:02:08,393 --> 00:02:09,690
above parallel reads.

49
00:02:10,650 --> 00:02:12,711
These polygons compare the methods

50
00:02:12,711 --> 00:02:14,469
across nine operation groups.

51
00:02:14,869 --> 00:02:17,234
The left chart normalizes each group

52
00:02:17,234 --> 00:02:19,928
to its best method. The right chart shows

53
00:02:19,928 --> 00:02:22,359
actual success rates. All values come

54
00:02:22,359 --> 00:02:24,725
from the complete Full50 evaluation.

55
00:02:26,650 --> 00:02:29,041
The qualitative examples pair the human

56
00:02:29,041 --> 00:02:31,739
reference with its recorded robot execution.

57
00:02:31,739 --> 00:02:33,455
First, pouring between cups.

58
00:02:36,650 --> 00:02:38,944
The same architecture also transfers

59
00:02:38,944 --> 00:02:41,749
the demonstrated procedure to hanging a mug.

60
00:02:46,650 --> 00:02:49,083
Folding and stowing requires multiple

61
00:02:49,083 --> 00:02:51,450
manipulation stages within one task.

62
00:02:56,650 --> 00:02:59,429
Finally, RoboDemo achieves seventy-three

63
00:02:59,429 --> 00:03:02,138
point three percent mean success across

64
